WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:09.060
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:15.484
Unit eight: Ethics in Sport. Today you will say who does the action with passive + 'by'.

4
00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:18.436
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.633
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.682
Fair competition.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:29.134
Fair competition means competing with the same rules for all.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.028
Fair competition makes sport exciting.

9
00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:35.397
Your turn. Say: Fair competition.

10
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:39.676
Fair competition.

11
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:42.451
Performance-enhancing drugs.

12
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:47.621
Performance-enhancing drugs means banned drugs that make athletes stronger.

13
00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:50.297
Performance-enhancing drugs are banned.

14
00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:54.453
Your turn. Say: Performance-enhancing drugs.

15
00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.241
Performance-enhancing drugs.

16
00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:01.066
Governing body.

17
00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.338
Governing body means the organisation that controls a sport.

18
00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.996
FIFA is football's governing body.

19
00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:11.805
Your turn. Say: Governing body.

20
00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:15.888
Governing body.

21
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.907
Ethical dilemma.

22
00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:22.217
Ethical dilemma means a hard choice between right and wrong.

23
00:01:22.817 --> 00:01:25.257
Reporting a friend is an ethical dilemma.

24
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:28.537
Your turn. Say: Ethical dilemma.

25
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.657
Ethical dilemma.

26
00:01:33.417 --> 00:01:34.952
Integrity clause.

27
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:39.842
Integrity clause means a part of a contract about honest behaviour.

28
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.972
Her contract has an integrity clause.

29
00:01:43.583 --> 00:01:46.259
Your turn. Say: Integrity clause.

30
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.716
Integrity clause.

31
00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.567
Whistleblower.

32
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:56.407
Whistleblower means a person who reports wrongdoing.

33
00:01:57.017 --> 00:01:59.097
The whistleblower exposed the cheating.

34
00:01:59.683 --> 00:02:02.185
Your turn. Say: Whistleblower.

35
00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:05.976
Whistleblower.

36
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:08.438
Code of conduct violation.

37
00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:13.017
Code of conduct violation means breaking the rules of behaviour.

38
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:15.779
Fighting is a code of conduct violation.

39
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:19.547
Your turn. Say: Code of conduct violation.

40
00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.632
Code of conduct violation.

41
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:26.872
Athlete accountability.

42
00:02:27.883 --> 00:02:32.008
Athlete accountability means athletes taking responsibility for actions.

43
00:02:32.617 --> 00:02:35.185
Athlete accountability builds respect.

44
00:02:35.783 --> 00:02:39.364
Your turn. Say: Athlete accountability.

45
00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.898
Athlete accountability.

46
00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.278
Institutional trust.

47
00:02:47.283 --> 00:02:50.664
Institutional trust means trust in organisations.

48
00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.784
Scandals damage institutional trust.

49
00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:57.361
Your turn. Say: Institutional trust.

50
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.095
Institutional trust.

51
00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.524
Transparency in sport.

52
00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:09.467
Transparency in sport means openness about decisions and rules.

53
00:03:10.083 --> 00:03:12.698
Transparency in sport stops corruption.

54
00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:16.249
Your turn. Say: Transparency in sport.

55
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.925
Transparency in sport.

56
00:03:21.683 --> 00:03:23.369
Moral responsibility.

57
00:03:24.383 --> 00:03:27.614
Moral responsibility means a duty to do the right thing.

58
00:03:28.217 --> 00:03:31.075
Coaches have a moral responsibility to players.

59
00:03:31.683 --> 00:03:35.067
Your turn. Say: Moral responsibility.

60
00:03:37.933 --> 00:03:39.689
Moral responsibility.

61
00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.335
Reform.

62
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.849
Reform means a change to make something better.

63
00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.078
The league needs reform.

64
00:03:47.683 --> 00:03:50.417
Your turn. Say: Reform.

65
00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:54.152
Reform.

66
00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:58.559
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:59.417 --> 00:04:01.811
Visal, what happens when athletes cheat?

68
00:04:02.917 --> 00:04:06.008
Violations are investigated by the governing body.

69
00:04:07.117 --> 00:04:08.373
Who discovers them?

70
00:04:09.483 --> 00:04:12.934
Often, cheating is reported by a whistleblower.

71
00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.214
And the punishment?

72
00:04:16.317 --> 00:04:21.790
Bans are decided by an independent panel. That builds institutional trust.

73
00:04:22.933 --> 00:04:24.817
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:25.683 --> 00:04:28.716
Grammar focus: Passive with by plus agent.

75
00:04:29.016 --> 00:04:30.145
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.871
Violations are investigated by the governing body.

77
00:04:34.783 --> 00:04:36.934
Cheating was reported by a whistleblower.

78
00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.418
Bans are decided by an independent panel.

79
00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:44.841
Add 'by' + agent when it is important to say who does the action.

80
00:04:45.583 --> 00:04:50.175
Be careful! Don't say: Violations are investigated from the governing body.

81
00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:56.060
Say: Violations are investigated by the governing body.

82
00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.476
Use 'by' for the agent in the passive.

83
00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:01.896
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.096
Clean Competition.

85
00:05:04.396 --> 00:05:06.767
Fair competition is the heart of sport.

86
00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:11.206
Performance-enhancing drugs are banned by every governing body.

87
00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.465
Violations are investigated by independent experts.

88
00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:19.476
Sometimes cheating is exposed by a brave whistleblower.

89
00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:23.743
Transparency and reform rebuild institutional trust.

90
00:05:24.833 --> 00:05:28.847
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:29.683 --> 00:05:32.623
Violations are investigated blank the governing body.

92
00:05:32.923 --> 00:05:35.799
A, by. B, from. C, with.

93
00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:41.205
The answer is A: by.

94
00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:44.860
A person who reports wrongdoing is a blank.

95
00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.907
A, whistleblower. B, referee. C, governor.

96
00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:54.617
The answer is A: whistleblower.

97
00:05:55.783 --> 00:05:58.886
A hard choice between right and wrong is an ethical blank.

98
00:05:59.186 --> 00:06:03.164
A, dilemma. B, reform. C, clause.

99
00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.769
The answer is A: dilemma.

100
00:06:09.967 --> 00:06:12.909
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:17.201
How should sports organizations handle ethical violations?

102
00:06:26.017 --> 00:06:27.459
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:27.759 --> 00:06:38.085
Violations should be investigated by an independent group. The results should be shared openly, so fans and athletes can trust the sport.

104
00:06:38.385 --> 00:06:40.815
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:41.717 --> 00:06:46.366
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and passive with by plus agent.

106
00:06:46.666 --> 00:06:50.526
Today's value is fair play. Play fairly and follow the rules.

107
00:06:50.826 --> 00:06:53.107
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

108
00:06:53.407 --> 00:06:56.628
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

